sway: window stacking — `lift_tiled_on_press` (peek), `pin`, `z raise|lower`, window:move for floating drag/resize (SWAY-6, SWAY-7; plan docs/akunito/plans/sway-waybar-per-monitor-and-zorder.md §3)

Peek: `lift_tiled_on_press enable|disable` (config + runtime, default off). A left or right press on the visible part of a TILE that a floating container overlaps draws that tile above the floating layer until the press ends. Only the tile under the button, one at a time, no delay; floating_modifier presses, the middle button, titlebar presses (seatop_default, not seatop_down) and workspaces with a fullscreen view never peek.
Design: new scene layer root->layers.lifted between floating and shell_top, plus root->lifted. Not a one-shot reparent: every transaction re-parents tiles into their workspace (arrange_children) and the lifting click itself commits one, so root_arrange_lifted() runs at the end of every arrange_root and moves the tile again, at the layout position arrange_children just gave it (wlr_scene_node_coords). When arrange did not lay it out as a visible tile (floated, fullscreen, workspace hidden, covered by a fullscreen view) the lift is dropped. Release is in seatop_down's .end, which seatop_end runs on every exit path (button release, surface destroy, unref, touch/tablet up, another seatop starting); it puts the node back into its parent's content tree (or the workspace tiling tree) at its relative position, and container_destroy clears a dangling root->lifted.

Pin: `pin enable|disable|toggle` on the toplevel floating container; enabling it on a tiled container fails ("Can only pin floating containers"), disabling always works. The pinned band is the tail of ws->floating: workspace_insert_floating_band() puts a floater at the top of its band and is used by workspace_add_floating (sticky floaters are re-added on every workspace switch and would otherwise land above the pinned ones) and container_raise_floating (focus, clicks, move/resize seatops, scratchpad show), which also places the scene node below the next floater of the list instead of raising it to the top. arrange_workspace_floating restores the list order in the scene per layer at its end (floaters of every workspace share root->layers.floating and reparenting to an unchanged parent is a no-op, so scene and list order drift); it touches the scene only when a node is not already right below the next one. Pin does not imply above_fullscreen: a pinned + above_fullscreen floater keeps its pin order inside the fullscreen layer. get_tree exposes "pinned" (the raw flag, like "sticky").

`z raise|lower`: swaps the toplevel floating container with its neighbour in ws->floating when both are in the same band; bottom stays bottom, the top of a band stays below the next band. Tiled -> error. With `bindsym --whole-window ... z raise` the target is the container under the cursor.

window:move IPC events: seatop_move_floating (finalize), seatop_resize_floating (button release) and the floating paths of the `resize` command now emit ipc_event_window(con, "move"), so floating geometry changes are observable without polling.

Applies with zero fuzz on sway 1.11 plus nixpkgs' patches, with or without sway-478-null-output-autoconfigure, sway-xwayland-zero-scaling and sway-above-fullscreen (all six combinations checked); in this repo it is applied after both local patches.

Measured 2026-10-14, nested headless sway 1.11 (pixman, 1280x720, DESK's patch stack + this patch), tests/e2e/test_30_stacking.py, pixel checks with grim on solid-colour GTK clients, input from a zwp_virtual_pointer / zwp_virtual_keyboard client: 7/7 pass (13/13 with the harness cases, 7.2 s). Same 13/13 on LAPTOP_X13's stack (nixpkgs patches + 478 + this patch only), where the fullscreen case is a no-op for lack of above_fullscreen.
- Peek: red tile + blue float at 100,100 400x300: pixel 300,250 blue; left press at 900,500 -> red while held, blue after release; same with the right button; held through a `gaps inner all set 4` transaction it stays red; `lift_tiled_on_press disable` -> stays blue. Middle button, and Alt (floating_modifier Mod1, tiling_drag disable so the press reaches seatop_down) -> stays blue for 0.3 s.
- Fullscreen: red fullscreen view + blue above_fullscreen float: a press on the fullscreen view keeps the float drawn (no lift).
- Pin: green pinned float stays above the blue normal float after clicking and focusing the blue one; floating_nodes order [normal, pinned]. A sticky normal float carried to a workspace whose pinned float is already there lands below it; still below after two more switches; sticky + pinned carried to workspace 3 stays on top; after `pin disable` a click raises the other float again. Without the band in workspace_add_floating the sticky case fails (blue on top): checked with a mutated build.
- z: three floats stacked at 200,200: `z lower` acb, twice more cab (bottom stays bottom), `z raise` cba; Hyper+button5 over the top float lowers it (cab), Hyper+button4 over the top one changes nothing; with c pinned (abc) `z raise` on b and `z lower` on c change nothing.
- Tiled: `pin enable`, `pin toggle`, `z raise` refused with "floating" in the error; `pin disable` accepted.
- IPC: Alt-drag 100,100 -> window:move with rect 200,150; Alt+right drag -> window:move; `resize set 350 250` -> window:move with 350x250.

